## Example Rule YAML: `rules/orders_not_null.yaml`

```yaml
rule_id: "orders_ship_date_not_null"
version: "1.0.0"
target:
  platform: snowflake
  table: "tpch.orders"
  columns: ["ship_date"]
quality_dimension: completeness
predicate: "ship_date IS NOT NULL"
severity: 3
enabled: true
shadow_mode: false
owner: "data-engineering@example.com"
description: "All orders must have a ship date"
```

## Example Manual Lineage: `lineage.yaml`

```yaml
- dataset: "tpch.orders"
  downstream_assets:
    - type: dashboard
      name: "Revenue Dashboard"
    - type: ml_model
      name: "shipment_delay_predictor"
    - type: reverse_etl
      name: "Salesforce Sync"
- dataset: "tpch.customer"
  downstream_assets:
    - type: dashboard
      name: "Customer Lifetime Value"
```

## How to Run

```bash
# Install PyYAML if not present
pip install pyyaml

# Compile rule
python datatrust_compiler.py rules/orders_not_null.yaml

# Estimate incident cost (e.g., incident lasted 2.5 hours)
python cost_model.py rules/orders_not_null.yaml lineage.yaml 2.5
```

